schema: "0.4"
id: ml5_js-04-edge-privacy-offline-accessibility
type: "interactive/model"
quality: high
solution: ml5_js
category: ml-ai
variant: edge-privacy-offline-accessibility
references:
  - "references/fim/overview/music-audio-ml/ml5_js.md"
  - "references/fim/solution/ml5_js.md"

prompt:
  system: |-
    You generate ml5.js browser ML artifacts for FIM evaluation. Output only one complete self-contained ASCII HTML document with inline CSS and JavaScript. Use p5.js plus ml5.js 1.x from CDN, and do not include Markdown fences or explanatory prose outside the artifact.
  text: |-
    Create the edge, privacy, offline, and accessibility integration case for ml5.js.

    Scenario:
    Build a local-first browser ML interface for a kiosk or assistive interaction demo. The artifact should show consent-first camera use, privacy-preserving inference, offline-aware model loading, accessibility controls, and graceful fallback when ml5 model assets cannot be fetched.

    Implementation requirements:
    - Use p5.js and ml5.js 1.x CDN imports. Use an appropriate ml5 model such as ml5.bodyPose("MoveNet"), ml5.handPose(), or ml5.imageClassifier("MobileNet") as the primary solution.
    - Do not use legacy ml5 0.x APIs such as poseNet, handpose, facemesh, styleTransfer, or callbacks with an error first argument.
    - Include a consent gate before camera or microphone access. The default state must be a nonblank local demo that does not request permissions until the user chooses live input.
    - Include model load state, backend state, and network/offline state panels with loading, ready, running, cached, offline fallback, failed, and permission-denied states.
    - Explain the realistic offline constraint: ml5 model weights often need network access on first load, so offline use requires a prior cache or locally bundled assets. Provide deterministic local fallback when assets are unavailable.
    - Include privacy controls: live input stays in the browser, no uploads, no telemetry, no analytics, no persistent recordings, no third-party API calls beyond declared model/CDN assets, and no secrets, API keys, tokens, cookies, or credentials.
    - Display confidence values, threshold decisions, stale-result warnings, and uncertainty states in text and visual form.
    - Include accessibility integration: keyboard-only operation, large touch targets, ARIA live status, captions or text alternatives for visual inference, high contrast mode, reduced motion mode, and camera-free sample mode.
    - Include edge fallback behavior for denied camera, missing microphone, blocked CDN, offline first load, cached/offline reload, empty model results, low confidence, slow devices, hidden tab, and unsupported WebGL or WASM.
    - Include cleanup hooks that stop detection loops, tracks, timers, and animation when paused, on page hide, or on teardown.
    - Output only the final artifact, with no commentary outside the artifact.
  provider_options:
    max_tokens: 8192
    temperature: 0.2
    top_p: 0.9

output:
  text_format: html
  artifact_kind: ml5js-edge-privacy-accessibility-demo
  formats:
    - format: html
  render_expectation: Interactive local-first browser ML interface that works with live input when available and a deterministic fallback when privacy, network, or device constraints block inference.

evaluation:
  checklist:
    - "Format validity: YAML parses under schema 0.4, all text is ASCII-only, and generated output is exactly one complete HTML document with no Markdown fences."
    - "ml5 API: Uses p5.js with a current ml5.js 1.x model as the primary solution and avoids legacy model names or error-first callbacks."
    - "Model load state: Shows loading, ready, running, cached, offline fallback, failed, permission-denied, and teardown states for model, backend, and network conditions."
    - "Confidence display: Shows confidence percentages, threshold decisions, stale-result warnings, and uncertainty states in visual and textual form."
    - "Privacy and secrets: Uses consent-first live input, keeps inference local, avoids uploads, telemetry, analytics, recordings, undeclared network calls, API keys, tokens, cookies, credentials, and secret placeholders."
    - "Fallback behavior: Handles denied permissions, blocked CDN, offline first load, cached reload, empty results, low confidence, slow devices, hidden tab, and unsupported WebGL or WASM with deterministic local mode."
    - "Accessibility and integration: Provides keyboard operation, ARIA live status, high contrast, reduced motion, touch targets, text alternatives, camera-free mode, and cleanup hooks."
  rubric:
    - name: "Format validity"
      weight: 30
      criteria: "The prompt YAML and generated HTML are parseable, ASCII-only, complete, and free of Markdown wrappers or unrelated prose."
    - name: "Semantic completeness"
      weight: 30
      criteria: "The artifact implements an edge/privacy/offline/accessibility ml5.js integration with consent, current APIs, model and network state, local fallback, confidence reporting, and cleanup."
    - name: "UX/model quality"
      weight: 25
      criteria: "The interface presents consent, privacy, offline state, accessibility controls, confidence, and degraded model behavior clearly enough for kiosk or assistive use."
    - name: "Robustness"
      weight: 15
      criteria: "The artifact handles denied permissions, blocked network, offline first load, cached reload, model errors, low confidence, hidden-page lifecycle, unsupported backends, and teardown without runtime failure."
  pass_conditions:
    - "Rubric weights are exactly Format validity 30, Semantic completeness 30, UX/model quality 25, and Robustness 15."
    - "Generated content is clearly aligned with ml5.js 1.x and p5.js and does not substitute TensorFlow.js direct APIs as the primary solution."
    - "Model load state, privacy, no secrets, fallback behavior, and confidence display checks are all satisfied."
    - "Rubric score is at least 80 out of 100 and no rubric dimension scores zero."

tags:
  - "fim"
  - "ml-ai"
  - "ml5_js"
  - "edge"
  - "privacy"
  - "offline"
  - "accessibility"
  - "local-first"
